id: pm-rust-crash-lock-restart
title: Recover incomplete native lock initialization after process death
description: "The first native lock fsync follows a complete owner payload but leaves a fresh empty publication gate on process death. That gate blocks existing confirmed-dead-owner recovery and causes update/comment restart exit 4 while acknowledged item/history bytes remain intact. Recover only under the kernel lease with verified same-host original-process death and identity-checked empty-gate reclamation. Preserve unknown/live-owner refusals, immutable histories, exact restart references and the 50-writer no-loss contract; builds on #104."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: crash-consistency,follow-up,locks
created_at: "2026-10-21T22:16:11.158Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T23:35:15.935Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T22:19:53.971Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: lock and initialization searches found no open item covering safe recovery from incomplete lock publication. This is distinct from text ownership refusal parity and completed owner-death locking work. The two measured failures are native update/comment at fsync ordinal 1, restart exit 4; all acknowledged item/history bytes remain intact. Repair policy is deliberately separate from the crash evidence harness."
  "2026-10-21T23:04:13.757Z",codex-agent,"Read both retained same-family update/comment fsync ordinal 1 cases and #104. The first fsync follows a complete owner-payload write; the fresh empty publication gate prevents the existing confirmed-dead-owner recovery. Plan: while holding the existing kernel lease, admit identity-checked empty-gate reclamation only for a confirmed dead same-host owner; retain TTL and unknown/live/nonempty-gate refusals. Add permanent independent replay cases, require every measured boundary to recover, and verify 50 simultaneous writers without Git. Targeted checks locally; unchanged-threshold release-check matrix remains the full CI gate. This branch builds on #104 and must merge after it."
  "2026-10-21T23:19:03.467Z",codex-agent,"The corrected synthetic corpus passes 20/20 injected kills with 20/20 acknowledged writes, history prefixes, exact reference states and restart receipts; both cross-runtime baseline byte and acknowledgement comparisons pass. The separate permanent update/comment first-fsync replay tests pass 2/2; the fresh-gate owner and lease guard unit test passes. The initial minimal fixture failed oracle settings validation and was corrected before proof. A default-budget standalone run timed out under local load; the supported 60000 ms process budget completed the corpus. No recovery invariant or coverage threshold was relaxed. Targeted Rust acceptance and behavioral revert proof are next."
  "2026-10-21T23:27:21.449Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof complete: replaced only mutation::acquire_lock_attempt with the #104 implementation, rebuilt using CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 cargo +1.90.0 build --locked --bin pm-rust, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern='retained (update|comment)' scripts/crash-harness.test.mts. Reverted: 0 passed, 2 failed, both actual restart exits 4. Restored and rebuilt: 2 passed, 0 failed. Tests and fixtures were unchanged. Full harness via the pinned PM linked runner passes 16/16 with zero skips; gate-focused unit selection passes 6/6; 50 writers preserve all 150 comments and the exact history chain. Shared-path ownership JSON refusal comparison passes exactly. The separate pre-existing comment diagnostic mismatch is retained on pm-rust-comment-lock-receipt; native legacy formatting is unchanged here. No PM CLI/SDK defect was identified."
  "2026-10-21T23:28:46.932Z",codex-agent,"Final pinned PM linked Rust acceptance passes: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --test concurrency_contract --test parity_1021_contract with CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 and PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 runs 2/2 concurrency tests plus 14/14 October 21 contract tests, zero failed or ignored. All 50 simultaneous writers retain 150/150 comments and history links without Git. Full harness 16/16, gate-focused unit selection 6/6 and restored independent replay tests 2/2 pass. Strict targeted Clippy, formatting, TypeScript checking, ESLint, changelog generation/check and immutable tracker-history prefix checks pass. Full unchanged-threshold release-check is delegated to the Linux/macOS/Windows CI matrix as requested; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T23:29:45.182Z",codex-agent,Local check-only health reports inherited history-chain warnings for pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih. An independent plain-directory archive of the unchanged #104 head reports the same warnings. Guidance/provenance/stale-item advisories and shared configuration drift also remain. No existing history was repaired or rewritten; the original restart-item stream remains an exact prefix of the appended history. CI's existing clone-local health setup remains authoritative for its gate. This is separate from the passing recovery and concurrency evidence.
  "2026-10-21T23:35:14.434Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and local verification are complete in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/105, based on main and explicitly dependent on #104 merging first. The final verification receipt will be kept in that PR with the exact-head CI run URL, per-platform test totals and all four coverage counts, linked from docs/CRASH_HARNESS.md. The Linux/macOS/Windows release-check matrix is still pending; no pending, canceled, skipped or unavailable reviewer result is treated as approval. Releasing the implementation claim for orchestrator verification while retaining in_progress status. No merge or release."
